{"name":"Vermeer Blue","hex":"#2b7caf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Johannes Vermeer","blocks":[{"text":"Johannes Vermeer was a Dutch painter who specialized in domestic interior scenes of middle-class life. He is considered one of the greatest painters of the Dutch Golden Age. During his lifetime, he was a moderately successful provincial genre painter, recognized in Delft and The Hague. He produced relatively few paintings, primarily earning his living as an art dealer. He was not wealthy; at his death, his wife was left in debt."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Cropped_version_of_Jan_Vermeer_van_Delft_002.jpg/330px-Cropped_version_of_Jan_Vermeer_van_Delft_002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johannes_Vermeer"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Jesuite_Kerk%2C_Abraham_Rademaker%2C_SA_Delft%2C_inv.nr._5691.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Jesuite_Kerk%2C_Abraham_Rademaker%2C_SA_Delft%2C_inv.nr._5691.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Jesuite_Kerk%2C_Abraham_Rademaker%2C_SA_Delft%2C_inv.nr._5691.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Jesuite_Kerk%2C_Abraham_Rademaker%2C_SA_Delft%2C_inv.nr._5691.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Jesuite_Kerk%2C_Abraham_Rademaker%2C_SA_Delft%2C_inv.nr._5691.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Jesuite_Kerk%2C_Abraham_Rademaker%2C_SA_Delft%2C_inv.nr._5691.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Jesuit Church on the Oude Langendijk in Delft, c. 1730, brush in gray ink, by Abraham Rademaker, coll. Stadsarchief Delft","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJesuite_Kerk%2C_Abraham_Rademaker%2C_SA_Delft%2C_inv.nr._5691.tif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2010-05-15-delft-by-RalfR-13.jpg/500px-2010-05-15-delft-by-RalfR-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2010-05-15-delft-by-RalfR-13.jpg/1280px-2010-05-15-delft-by-RalfR-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/2010-05-15-delft-by-RalfR-13.jpg/500px-2010-05-15-delft-by-RalfR-13.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Replica of